+# Existing installed disk cold boot — candidate, mock-tested only
+
+Root integration/review required. Do not run until installation completed, clean guest shutdown and QEMU exit are verified, and owner offline qcow2 inspection establishes installed target identity, format, layout/bootblocks, no backing chain, and clean state. This candidate deliberately has no disk creation/reset, installer, ISO, snapshot, arbitrary arguments, or success-assertion path.
+
+Run Python 3.11+ as root **on the Linux daemon host**, in its initial PID namespace. Requires existing Docker CLI, sha256sum/stat in pinned image, and local ext4/XFS/Btrfs storage. Canonical absolute paths only. No SSH/client-path translation. Example placeholders are not a launch authorization:
+
+```sh
+python3 coldboot.py --disk /ABSOLUTE/EXISTING/install.qcow2 \
+  --firmware /ABSOLUTE/openbios-sparc64.patched \
+  --qemu /ABSOLUTE/qemu-system-sparc64.candidate \
+  --evidence /ABSOLUTE/PARENT/NEW-UNIQUE-coldboot-evidence \
+  --offline-clean-shutdown-confirmed --exclusive-host-confirmed --deadline 2100
+```
+
+Evidence directory must not exist; parent must exist. The two required confirmations attest clean offline installation and operator-exclusive host/disk ownership for the entire session. Without those facts, do not supply them. Root must prevent concurrent raw writes/path replacement. The harness checks `/proc` visibility, refuses **any** other opener (including readers), takes a cooperating sidecar flock without writing disk bytes, rechecks before start, and requests QEMU native `file.locking=on`. QEMU locking closes a normal cooperating QEMU writer race; it cannot exclude arbitrary raw writers ignoring locks. Sidecar lock is retained until verified cleanup finishes, then released. If stop cannot be verified, outcome is incomplete; do not retry or start another writer.
+
+Fixed unix Docker socket, kernel boot-ID comparison and device/inode/size comparison inside the mounted runtime reject host/daemon identity mismatch before QEMU. QEMU and firmware are hashed on host AND mounted runtime. Container creation uses `--pull=never` and pinned image ID; QEMU exec occurs only after runtime checks. This does not prove safety against a malicious daemon/root or replacement after final check. Docker commands have client timeouts; an unreachable daemon can outlive client timeout, so unresolved creation/stop remains incomplete and needs owner reconciliation. CID file plus UUID label are required for cleanup; never stop by guessed name, never remove any container.
+
+Interactive stdin is forwarded to guest serial. Raw merged serial/runtime stderr goes to `console.log`; tail that file from a separate local terminal. No boot commands are auto-injected. At fresh firmware prompt, operator captures `dev /aliases` then `.properties` and verifies `disk` resolves to this sole IDE index0 installed target. Full path/slice remains unverified; do not invent aliases or `:a`. Apply original serial path check and workarounds:
+
+```text
+dev /pci@1f,0/pci@1,1/ebus@1/power@14,7240
+" interrupts" delete-property
+dev /pci@1f,0/pci@1,1/ebus@1/fdthree@0,0
+" fdthree-disabled" device-name
+boot disk -v
+```
+
+Last command remains conditional on verified alias. Disk-only `-boot c`, no ISO mount or CD device, candidate compatibility ON, firmware132,1088MiB/1CPU/2GiB. Default QEMU disk cache behavior is unchanged; no snapshot/write-discard mode. Serial transport differs from installation's UNIX socket (stdio here); monitor disabled. No automatic guest input or changes to firmware device topology.
+
+Owner should cleanly shut down the guest before deadline. At deadline, cap, cancellation or failure, exact owned container is stopped (10s grace, then bounded kill if required); forced shutdown can leave installed filesystem dirty. Preserve disk and inspect; never call that clean. Capture login, installed root identity and ISO absence for review; writable persistence/reboot are separate proofs. No automatic PASS: even client exit0 returns `UNVERIFIED_SESSION_END` with process exit2. Inspect includes guest exit/OOM/running state. Error and timeout are incomplete.
+
+Console threshold64MiB, maximum read overshoot65535 bytes; Docker logging can continue briefly during bounded cleanup and has separate daemon storage overhead. Session2100s maximum, Docker operations30s each (stop20s,kill10s), client termination5+5s; cleanup inspection can add several bounded commands. This is not a2100s whole-program wall-clock guarantee. Preserve `preflight.json`, `start.json`, `console.log`, `owned.cid`, `outcome.json`, stopped retained container and installed disk. Outcome is also printed if evidence writing fails. No disk hash is taken while running. No broad cleanup.
+
+Tests: `python3 -m unittest -v test_coldboot.py`; all subprocess Docker paths mocked. No actual runtime, filesystem locking, mount option, console or installed coldboot validation claimed.
